@@ -224,6 +224,12 @@ const CREDENTIALING_CHECKLIST = [
 
 /* Newest first. Add new entries at the top. */
 const DOCUMENT_LOG = [
+  {
+    date: "September 23, 2026",
+    time: "10:28 AM EDT",
+    document: "Anesthesiology — Physician DOP, case log, and privileging guide (September 23, 2026)",
+    change: "Replaced the May 18, 2026 Anesthesiology (Physician) DOP with Anesthesia_Physician_Sept_23_2026.pdf and the July 8, 2026 physician case-log template with ANESTHESIA_(PHYSICIAN)_CASE_LOG_TEMPLATE_Sept_23_2026.xlsx. Age-based privileges on the DOP were restructured: removed the prior “2 months of age and older” / “&lt;2 months of age” split and the Adult (18+) vs Pediatric (2 months–17 years) website blocks; the form and guide now use three age bands — (1) 2 months to less than 24 months (Additional Requirements: ACGME-/AOA-accredited pediatric anesthesiology fellowship or Medical Staff Bylaws equivalent, AND current PALS), (2) 2 years to less than 13 years (Additional Requirement: current PALS only), and (3) 13 years of age and older (no age-specific additional requirements beyond core anesthesiology education, ABA/AOBA certification with ACLS and/or PeRLS, and the 50/12 and 150/36 encounter volume rules). Pediatric anesthesiology board certification is no longer listed as a separate website requirement for the youngest band. The case-log workbook was simplified from separate Adult Anesthesia and Pediatric Anesthesia sheets to a single Cases sheet (Patient Age remains a column so age-band activity can still be documented). Updated FILE_GROUPS and DOCUMENT_LOG on this Admin page, and updated DOP_FORM, CASE_LOG, and DATA.anesthesia_physician on index.html so downloads and the interactive requirements summary match the new documents."
+  },
   {
     date: "August 13, 2026",
     time: "9:20 AM EDT",
